  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a Tree Survey/ Arboricultural Report / Method Statements, the applicant has failed to satisfactorily demonstrate that the proposal would not lead to damage or loss of trees of amenity value in the vicinity of the site fails. The proposal would not therefore comply with the requirements of Policy LP51 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (LP33).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its size, design and position, would result in an undue overbearing impact and loss of outlook which would result in an unacceptable adverse impact on the amenity of the neighbouring occupiers. As such the proposed development is contrary to policies D3 (Optimising Site Capacity through the Design-led Approach) D6 (Housing Quality and Standards) of the London Plan 2021, policy LP2 (Development and Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and the guidance contained within Hackney Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD 2009.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed extension, by reason of its size, design and siting, would appear as a cramped and incongruous form of development, detrimental to the character and appearance of the host building and the wider conservation area. Therefore, the proposal does not meet the requirements of London Plan policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), HC1 (Heritage conservation and growth) and Hackney Local Plan policies LP1 (Design quality and local character) and LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of lack of provision of affordable housing, would fail to adequately contribute towards the provision of mixed and balanced communities and housing need in the local area. As such, the development would not be consistent with Policies H4 and H5 of the London Plan (2021), Hackney Local Plan Policies LP12, LP13 and NPPF (2024) paragraph 63 and the Hackney S106 Planning Contributions Supplementary Planning Document (2020).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The application fails to provide adequate information to demonstrate how the proposed development would deliver measurable Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG) or be exempt from the requirements, contrary to the requirements set out in the Environment Act 2021. In the absence of this information, the Local Planning Authority cannot determine the impact on local biodiversity or ensure compliance with Policy LP47 of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (LP33), and Paragraph 187 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by reason of a lack of sufficient energy efficiency measures and/or financial contribution towards carbon offsetting, would fail to achieve the maximum feasible reductions in carbon dioxide emissions, contrary to Hackney Local Plan (LP33) Policy LP55 and London Plan (2021) Policy SI2.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;In the absence of a suitable undertaking to secure that the occupiers of the new residential units would not be able to apply for on street parking permit, the proposals would have an adverse impact on street parking conditions, highway safety and sustainable modes of transport, contrary to Policies T1 and T4 of the London Plan (2021) and Hackney Local Plan Policies LP43 and LP45.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
